## Impact
| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| Severity | Medium — ReDoS via malicious input text |
| Affected | Canvas widget syntax parsing, chat canvas rendering |
| Attack vector | Send text crafted to trigger exponential regex backtracking (e.g., 'aaaaaaaaaaaaab') |

## Fix
Use regex with atomic groups or possessive quantifiers where possible. Set regex timeouts. Validate input length before regex. Consider using RE2-compatible patterns.

## Reproduction
1. Send text 'a'.repeat(100000) + 'b' to canvas renderer
2. Observe event loop blocked for minutes/hours

## References
- ReDoS (Regular Expression Denial of Service)
- OWASP ReDoS prevention

## What happens
Buffer operations (`Buffer.from`, `Buffer.alloc`) are used on user-controlled content without size validation. An attacker can supply extremely large payloads causing memory exhaustion (OOM) or excessive memory allocation.

