Closes #180756.

## What Problem This Solves

Operators cannot find an earlier error or identifier in the Web terminal's retained canvas output without manually scrolling or repeating commands.

## User Impact

The active terminal gains **Find**, match counts, previous/next navigation and a highlighted text preview. Finding a match scrolls the real terminal to its retained row without sending search text to the shell.

Search is literal, case-sensitive and limited to individual retained visual rows. Refresh or navigation rescans after new output; phrases spanning soft-wrapped rows and evicted output are outside this scope.

## Why This Change Was Made

Read the active Ghostty buffer directly, including full graphemes and explicitly printed spaces, without keeping a second output store or changing retention/protocol. A floating control preserves PTY geometry and leaves native selection/copy ownership alone. Each tab switch retires the search view.

## Evidence

Real Bash PTY → Web terminal/Ghostty → visible Find → actual viewport readback passed at the product head below. The early marker moved into scrollback and Find scrolled back to it; search emitted no PTY input. A subsequent ordinary command entered through the UI reached Bash and its output was read back.

